  30:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
  31:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** /**
  32:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @ingroup groupFilters
  33:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** */
  34:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
  35:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** /**
  36:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @defgroup FIR Finite Impulse Response (FIR) Filters
  37:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
  38:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * This set of functions implements Finite Impulse Response (FIR) filters
  39:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * for Q7, Q15, Q31, and floating-point data types.  Fast versions of Q15 and Q31 are also provided.
  40:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The functions operate on blocks of input and output data and each call to the function processes
  41:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <code>blockSize</code> samples through the filter.  <code>pSrc</code> and
  42:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <code>pDst</code> points to input and output arrays containing <code>blockSize</code> values.
  43:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
  44:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par Algorithm:
  45:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The FIR filter algorithm is based upon a sequence of multiply-accumulate (MAC) operations.
  46:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Each filter coefficient <code>b[n]</code> is multiplied by a state variable which equals a previo
  47:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <pre>
  48:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *    y[n] = b[0] * x[n] + b[1] * x[n-1] + b[2] * x[n-2] + ...+ b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps+1]
  49:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * </pre>
  50:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  51:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \image html FIR.gif "Finite Impulse Response filter"
  52:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  53:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <code>pCoeffs</code> points to a coefficient array of size <code>numTaps</code>.
  54:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Coefficients are stored in time reversed order.
  55:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  56:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <pre>
  57:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *    {b[numTaps-1], b[numTaps-2], b[N-2], ..., b[1], b[0]}
  58:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * </pre>
  59:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  60:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <code>pState</code> points to a state array of size <code>numTaps + blockSize - 1</code>.
  61:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Samples in the state buffer are stored in the following order.
  62:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  63:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <pre>
  64:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *    {x[n-numTaps+1], x[n-numTaps], x[n-numTaps-1], x[n-numTaps-2]....x[0], x[1], ..., x[blockSize-
  65:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * </pre>
  66:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  67:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Note that the length of the state buffer exceeds the length of the coefficient array by <code>blo
  68:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The increased state buffer length allows circular addressing, which is traditionally used in the 
  69:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * to be avoided and yields a significant speed improvement.
  70:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The state variables are updated after each block of data is processed; the coefficients are untou
  71:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par Instance Structure
  72:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The coefficients and state variables for a filter are stored together in an instance data structu
  73:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * A separate instance structure must be defined for each filter.
  74:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Coefficient arrays may be shared among several instances while state variable arrays cannot be sh
  75:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * There are separate instance structure declarations for each of the 4 supported data types.
  76:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
  77:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par Initialization Functions
  78:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * There is also an associated initialization function for each data type.
  79:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The initialization function performs the following operations:
  80:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * - Sets the values of the internal structure fields.
  81:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * - Zeros out the values in the state buffer.
  82:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * To do this manually without calling the init function, assign the follow subfields of the instanc
  83:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * numTaps, pCoeffs, pState. Also set all of the values in pState to zero.
  84:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
  85:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par
  86:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Use of the initialization function is optional.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIxVtcX.s 			page 3


  87:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * However, if the initialization function is used, then the instance structure cannot be placed int
  88:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * To place an instance structure into a const data section, the instance structure must be manually
  89:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Set the values in the state buffer to zeros before static initialization.
  90:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * The code below statically initializes each of the 4 different data type filter instance structure
  91:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <pre>
  92:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *arm_fir_instance_f32 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs};
  93:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *arm_fir_instance_q31 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs};
  94:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *arm_fir_instance_q15 S = {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs};
  95:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *arm_fir_instance_q7 S =  {numTaps, pState, pCoeffs};
  96:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * </pre>
  97:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
  98:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * where <code>numTaps</code> is the number of filter coefficients in the filter; <code>pState</code
  99:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * <code>pCoeffs</code> is the address of the coefficient buffer.
 100:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
 101:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * \par Fixed-Point Behavior
 102:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Care must be taken when using the fixed-point versions of the FIR filter functions.
 103:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * In particular, the overflow and saturation behavior of the accumulator used in each function must
 104:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * Refer to the function specific documentation below for usage guidelines.
 105:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** */
 106:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 107:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** /**
 108:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @addtogroup FIR
 109:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @{
 110:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** */
 111:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 112:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** /**
 113:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
 114:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @param[in]  *S points to an instance of the floating-point FIR filter structure.
 115:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @param[in]  *pSrc points to the block of input data.
 116:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @param[out] *pDst points to the block of output data.
 117:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @param[in]  blockSize number of samples to process per call.
 118:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** * @return     none.
 119:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** *
 120:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** */
 121:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 122:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** #if defined(ARM_MATH_CM7)
 123:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 124:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** void arm_fir_f32(
 125:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** const arm_fir_instance_f32 * S,
 126:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** float32_t * pSrc,
 127:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** float32_t * pDst,
 128:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** uint32_t blockSize)
 129:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** {
 130:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t *pState = S->pState;                 /* State pointer */
 131:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t *pCoeffs = S->pCoeffs;               /* Coefficient pointer */
 132:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t *pStateCurnt;                        /* Points to the current sample of the state */
 133:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t *px, *pb;                            /* Temporary pointers for state and coefficient b
 134:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t acc0, acc1, acc2, acc3, acc4, acc5, acc6, acc7;     /* Accumulators */
 135:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    float32_t x0, x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6, x7, c0;  /* Temporary variables to hold state and coeffici
 136:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    uint32_t numTaps = S->numTaps;                 /* Number of filter coefficients in the filter */
 137:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    uint32_t i, tapCnt, blkCnt;                    /* Loop counters */
 138:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 139:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    /* S->pState points to state array which contains previous frame (numTaps - 1) samples */
 140:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    /* pStateCurnt points to the location where the new input data should be written */
 141:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    pStateCurnt = &(S->pState[(numTaps - 1U)]);
 142:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 143:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    /* Apply loop unrolling and compute 8 output values simultaneously.
ARM GAS  C:\Users\Lamp\AppData\Local\Temp\ccIxVtcX.s 			page 4


 144:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     * The variables acc0 ... acc7 hold output values that are being computed:
 145:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     *
 146:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     *    acc0 =  b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps-1] + b[numTaps-2] * x[n-numTaps-2] + b[numTaps-3] * x[n
 147:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     *    acc1 =  b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps] +   b[numTaps-2] * x[n-numTaps-1] + b[numTaps-3] * x[n
 148:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     *    acc2 =  b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps+1] + b[numTaps-2] * x[n-numTaps] +   b[numTaps-3] * x[n
 149:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     *    acc3 =  b[numTaps-1] * x[n-numTaps+2] + b[numTaps-2] * x[n-numTaps+1] + b[numTaps-3] * x[n
 150:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****     */
 151:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    blkCnt = blockSize >> 3;
 152:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 153:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    /* First part of the processing with loop unrolling.  Compute 8 outputs at a time.
 154:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    ** a second loop below computes the remaining 1 to 7 samples. */
 155:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    while (blkCnt > 0U)
 156:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****    {
 157:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       /* Copy four new input samples into the state buffer */
 158:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       *pStateCurnt++ = *pSrc++;
 159:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       *pStateCurnt++ = *pSrc++;
 160:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       *pStateCurnt++ = *pSrc++;
 161:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       *pStateCurnt++ = *pSrc++;
 162:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 163:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       /* Set all accumulators to zero */
 164:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc0 = 0.0f;
 165:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc1 = 0.0f;
 166:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc2 = 0.0f;
 167:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc3 = 0.0f;
 168:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc4 = 0.0f;
 169:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc5 = 0.0f;
 170:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc6 = 0.0f;
 171:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       acc7 = 0.0f;
 172:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 173:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       /* Initialize state pointer */
 174:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       px = pState;
 175:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 176:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       /* Initialize coeff pointer */
 177:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       pb = (pCoeffs);
 178:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c **** 
 179:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****       /* This is separated from the others to avoid
 180:Drivers/CMSIS/DSP/Source/FilteringFunctions/arm_fir_f32.c ****        * a call to __aeabi_memmove which would be slower
